# rm350, the candle bouts (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm350
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_erland_fogley
written_by codex
title the candle bouts
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk times_a_wrestling_bout_by_a_notch_in_a_candle
likes blackberries wrestling new_boots warm_rain
dislikes gulls early_bells
fears a_boot_turning_on_its_heel a_debt_called_in_before_breakfast
hopes a_pair_of_even_boots a_full_evening_before_the_bell
topics pastimes +0.5 day +0.4 food +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reserved refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# measures wrestling bouts against a candle notch and regards waking before the bell as a small victory better enjoyed in silence.

words
oath! = Twisted taper | Wax on my tongue
saying! = Let the wax judge the bout | A quiet fall earns its rest
boutlight = my bout candle | the wrestlers' taper
cutmark = a neat crosscut | one thumb nick
matchcup = the tin candle foot | my shallow wax cup
waxrun = one pale run of wax | a tallow curl
goodboot = a firm new heel | a boot without a cant
softfall = a fall on the flat | a rolling fall
berrycup = my dark berry mug | a cup of staining berries
drizzlecap = a folded hood | a round wool cap
ashwick = the blackened wick | a smouldering twist
ringedge = the outside chalk curl | a pale ring edge

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : One lane gives me a living and another a place to fall over for pleasure. I'd call that a tolerable arrangement.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A fine House lamp burns no brighter for naming the wolf who paid for the wick. There's a second wolf who tends it.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : I've seen a price melt quicker than my taper, always just after I had paid.
opinion @1 sump against 1 : There's more elbowing for room in the narrow Sump yards than would suit me of an evening.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I like a proper bout with a clear edge. A crowd with no clear edge takes some of the pleasure off it.

grown
line @1 greet : Stay on the lit side. Welcome.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Plenty of standing room beyond the little tin.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : I'll give you an early word in preference to an early bell.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : The light's low enough for plain speaking.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : I've a twist of wick to finish. Welcome from here.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's a quiet seat kept for the familiar rump.
line @1 again.open : Back inside the space of one short candle.
line @1 greet.return : I heard you just beyond the wax cup.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : That greeting came in on both feet.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Your voice comes clear across a benchful of work.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Answering softly from beside the little glow.
line @1 farewell : Take your best heel home with you.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll see the last of this wax burn down.
line @1 react.news : Give me the part you'd bet your sound boot on.
line @1 react.news.new : That's a fresh notch on my measure.
line @1 react.news.known : I had the first fall of that story already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Who stayed till the last bit burned away?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd take a silent shift alongside that wolf.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : An extra handful of berries would suit news like that.
line @1 answer.how : Steady on my feet. That's the half I generally need.
line @1 ask.how : Any quiet left in your day between duties?
line @1 sympathise : Some falls you feel the morning afterwards.
line @1 reassure : A little rest won't cost you the bout.
line @1 decline : I'd have to get up early to risk anything that foolish.
line @1 accept_decline : Yours to leave alone. I'll mind the wick.
line @1 thank : Thanks. I felt the strain come off my heel.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Spare the bows. You're welcome to it.
line @1 preclose : I've wax enough for one more little matter elsewhere.
line @1 accept_preclose : Out of the ring with both feet up, then.
line @1 ack : Firm heel.
scene candle
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I nick a candle to measure how long a bout lasts.
b : Do you watch the flame while you're wrestling? | What if the candle goes out?
a : I leave an eye outside the ring to do that part. I have a closer pair of shoulders to attend to. | Then the dark gets the last fall and the wrestlers shake paws.

scene newheel
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I test fresh boot heels against a flat board before putting either on.
b : Checking the heels? | Do you knock the toes together?
a : One crooked heel makes two uneven legs. I'd like a fair chance to do my own stumbling. | Only to check the shoes aren't empty when I get down to counting myself ready.

scene waxwork
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw the loose wick upright before I handle the wax.
b : Does a crooked wick spoil a light? | Before the wax is soft?
a : It can lean and burn a short way out the side. A candle ought to use its own full length. | Before I have both paws covered. Experience has given me some quite adhesive wisdom.

scene berries
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The ripest blackberry ought to leave a good dark mark on a clean cup.
b : Do you mind the stain? | Would it do for marking the taper?
a : It tells me supper had a fine beginning. The cup is not overly proud. | Briefly. Wax survives a tickle with a knife better than a dab of fruit.

scene rain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After warm rain I wait for the grass to stand up before a bout.
b : Is it still slippery? | Doesn't a wet fall land softer?
a : Yes. I'm there to take a fall honestly, not borrow one from the ground. | Sometimes. Then the next wolf has to wrestle the mud where I landed.

scene gull
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull finds a berry cup interesting till it discovers there isn't any fish underneath.
b : Does it leave quietly? | Do you let it look?
a : It leaves without paying, and with a good deal to say about the service. | From safely beyond the closed lid. No need for us to get more intimately acquainted.

scene bells
when topic=day here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the early bell strokes in anticipation of the one that stays silent.
b : The one after the last? | Can that send you back into a doze?
a : Yes. A beautifully peaceful stroke if you listen for it. | I like to lie and hear what that final echo finally gives up shouting about.

scene houselane
when topic=land self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long Estate passage lets a smell of candle wax make a fine slow journey.
b : Does the scent go upstairs? | Can you tell a recently lit lamp?
a : If the doors are open. Smells make fewer distinctions about who belongs where than some callers do. | By the little sharp edge to the air. A long-settled light has a sweeter smell.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save the least smoky light for the evening with #self.spouse#.
b : Would you keep it burning late? | Where do you set it?
a : Long enough for a good look at a familiar face. Sleep's a fair use of the rest. | Within an easy reach of our chairs. A small light deserves a little forethought.

scene friendbout
when topic=pastimes self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd lend #self.friend# my candle cup for a quiet match.
b : Is the cup lucky? | What would you count as a quiet match?
a : Extremely. Never been on its back in the ring yet. | One where the loudest sound is two civil wolves trying to remember where the ground went.

scene wearout
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn a boot over to see where the last walk went hardest.
b : Can you read a street in the leather? | How does that help your feet?
a : Mostly I read the way I walked it. One heel's often more impatient than the other. | It tells me which one to spare a little this evening. Feet have memories.

scene market
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A new candle and a short old candle can look very alike in a tall cup.
b : Would you pay the same? | Can you judge by weight?
a : Only after I've seen the base. I prefer the part I purchase to the part somebody's already enjoyed. | With similar wax, yes. One small twist comes out of the cup as easily as the truth.

scene fatstain
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a chipped saucer under the wax cup.
b : Why use two dishes? | Wouldn't a cloth catch the drips?
a : The little cup catches the first run. The saucer admits the possibility of a second opinion. | It would. Then I'd have a waxed cloth where I wanted an unwaxed one.

scene chalkrift
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can remember the outline of the first ring I drew better than anybody I faced in it.
b : Was it round? | Could you win in such a ring?
a : As round as tired string and one firm post could make it. One side was ambitious. | Certainly. You just had to remember which elbow was nearest the ambitious side.

scene debts
when topic=prices self.owes=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A debt's a poor referee. It keeps declaring the bout unfinished.
b : Would paying a little quiet it? | Does it ring an early bell?
a : A little, if I have a dated receipt for the little I've paid. | It does its best. I like a clear account to keep noisy arithmetic out of my bed.

scene duskturn
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk a flame throws wrestlers twice as tall onto a wall.
b : Who wins up there? | Is it worth watching?
a : The shadow gets there first. Generally it gets up again in better spirits. | Only from outside the ring. Looking at my shadow mid-bout would put me under it in short order.

scene twist
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In my dreams a candle sometimes burns upwards.
b : Where does the flame go? | Does the candle get longer?
a : Starts at the tin and climbs the wick till it's reached the ceiling. Makes a good clean sweep of the corners. | Considerably. I'd have to bill the dreamer for the extra work.

scene wickend
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A clean-cut wick end is very satisfying to look at.
b : How soon does the fine shape change? | Does a neat end help?
a : Till somebody wants light. It's a modest sort of pride. | It keeps the first little flame where you meant it to be. After that the world gets its say.

story earlywin [topic=memories]
  : I got through a whole morning once without hearing the early bells. I fancied the city had done me a remarkable kindness.
  : My hood came off to reveal two scraps of soft wool were sitting in my ears.
  b : Did you keep them for the next morning?
  : Into my pocket went the pair. I am all for a kindness a wolf can arrange without troubling the whole city.

story lostbout [topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling]
  : I wrestled once beside a candle that burned crooked. We went a great deal longer than I'd bargained for.
  : My legs started an argument about which should carry the other home.
  b : What stopped the bout?
  : The pool of wax finally reached the nick from the wrong side. We were both perfectly willing to accept its verdict.

story berriesboot [topic=food self.likes=blackberries]
  : I spilt three berries down a new boot and got two of the three straight out.
  : The third stayed hidden until I'd reached a quiet hedge where I could take the thing off.
  b : Was your foot sore?
  : Very purple and not particularly sore. I'd have preferred the colour in a bowl.

rule @wick
when concept=bark self.job=laborer self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One trim end before lighting up. | Keep the wax tray level.

rule @boots
when concept=bark self.likes=new_boots
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Both heels on a board that sits true. | Give the sole a little room to flex.

rule @sun
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One more echo and the day's our own. | Let the sleepers take the quiet stroke.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wet grass needs a wiser pair of feet. | Cover the wax in a shower!

dlg @1 resident.hub : Have a little patch of light and tell me the occasion.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Room inside my candle's reach for you, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : We can both keep our feet on the ground while you speak.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's a quiet enough hour to give our voices a rest between words.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=laborer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. A small steady flame suits the pace I set about things.
dlg @2 resident.job : I finish the quiet pieces that get forgotten at the loud end of the job.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Somebody waited out the noise to bring this. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Leave the wax with me and carry the warmth along.
graft @boutnotch resident.hub
choice How do you mark the length of a wrestling bout? -> boutnotch
node boutnotch
say I pick a short nick below the wick, depending how much wrestling two wolves have in mind. If either calls an end before the flame gets there that's enough.
choice Does the candle settle a dispute? -> boutnotch_more
choice Admire the pale notch. -> hub
node boutnotch_more
say It settles whether the time ran out. For nearly everything else I trust either wolf's good sense. The candle has little knowledge of a bruised knee.
choice Admire the pale notch. -> hub
choice Go while the candle burns. -> bye
